# Line endings are normalised in the repository, so a checkout is identical on Linux CI and on a
# Windows developer machine regardless of anyone's local core.autocrlf setting. Without this file
# the committed line endings depend on who ran `git add`, which is exactly the kind of hidden
# machine state the clean-setup experiment in results/ exists to remove.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must keep LF even when checked out on Windows: a CRLF shebang line is not runnable.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary-ish assets git should never try to normalise.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.trx binary
